0004-gas-rows-from-openimcc-janaf.patch
=======================================

Replace the JANAF-fitted gas rows for 35 species using openimcc d2a7516
(src/openimcc/data/gas/gas-shomate.csv). Na2O(g) and K2O(g) are excluded:
their openimcc provenance is LH84 plus NASA-Cp, not JANAF. Receipts:
docs-private/research/2026-09-29-imcc-retirement/gas-table-receipts.md and
docs-private/research/2026-10-01-vaporock-gas-0004/findings.md.

The per-species imported window is the union of source intervals: 22 species
have 500–1500 K and 1500–3000 K rows, 12 have only 1500–3000 K rows, and Cr(g)
has 1500–2900 K. Base rows are split at source bounds; existing coefficients
remain outside imported windows except in the nine declared gaps below. Six
source-only species are not imported because they have no parent oxide in
VapoRock's melt model and cannot be used by its equilibrium engine. Prior
effective behavior below 500 K is preserved for base species; this includes
original large JANAF errors at low temperatures.

Nine gaps use the fit having smaller maximum absolute error on the published
JANAF grid strictly inside each gap, independent of seam jumps and battery
residuals. Old-high/imported errors (J/mol):
  CaO 105.097069/1310.101024 (old); Fe 1.138733/0.486690 (imported);
  FeO 6.318010/39.982709 (old); MgO 3.110035/552.588095 (old);
  Si 1.923349/1.334765 (imported); SiO2 2.264821/4.384827 (old);
  Ti 1.482656/2.020629 (old); TiO 43.295557/30.000200 (imported);
  TiO2 3.131162/1.880397 (imported). Cr's retained base fit supplies
2900–3000 K, outside the nine declared gaps.

VapoRock selects rows with T > T_min and T <= T_max. It extends every row
whose T_min equals the species minimum to 0 K, and every row whose T_max
equals the species maximum to 1e8 K. The generated table has strict,
contiguous intervals and unique extrema, so only each species' first row
gets the lower extension and only its last row gets the upper extension.

Based on VapoRock 0159678a after patches 0001–0003.
